-- title:
--   A congruence subgroup of finite index in the r-unit group
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a,b$ and let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the rational quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of `IsOrder`: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and it is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Let $r$ be a natural number carrying a primality fact, let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose ideal contains the image of $r$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \neq r$. Write $\mathrm{awayUnits}(R,v)$ for the subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}$ consisting of those units whose image in $(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_w)^{\times}$, for every height-one prime $w \neq v$, lies in the subgroup generated by the units that, together with their inverses, lie in the local box of $R$ at $w$. The assertion is that there exists a subgroup $K$ of $\mathrm{awayUnits}(R,v)$ which is normal and of finite index, and such that every $\gamma \in K$ can be written as $\gamma = 1 + \ell\, y$ for some $y \in \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ with $r^{k} y \in R$ for some natural number $k$.
--
--   This provides a principal-congruence-type normal subgroup of finite index in the $r$-unit group of a quaternion order: its elements are congruent to $1$ modulo $\ell$ inside $R[1/r]$. It is used in the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfeld coset graph, where it feeds into [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.exists_normal_finiteIndex_forall_isOfFinOrder_imp_eq_one`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.exists_normal_finiteIndex_forall_isOfFinOrder_imp_eq_one) to produce a torsion-free normal subgroup of finite index.
